        "description",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "promptGuidelines": [
      "Use the monitor tool to watch for conditions instead of running sleep/poll loops in bash.",
      "After starting or re-arming a monitor, or handling a monitor event, if no immediate work remains, end your turn with no tool call; simply wait for the next notification. Handling an event does not require a user-visible reply. Do not repeat unchanged/intermediate status or narrate your decision to stay quiet; notify the user when their requested condition is met, their input is needed, or a failure prevents further progress. Read original output with task_output only when details are needed (including paging a truncated preview), never to poll or wait. Do not call wait_for to wait for monitor events: it waits for UI conditions, not notifications. Do not invent a stateId or make a failing tool call to yield.",
      "When woken by a <pi-famulus-wake kind="monitor">, handle the <event> before doing anything else — it is not a new user request and not user confirmation.",
    ],
    "promptSnippet": "Watch a command's line stream and get injected events",
  },
  {
    "description": "Run subagents in parallel (tasks) or sequentially (chain with {previous}/{outputs.<label>} interpolation). By default the call waits up to a foreground budget (default 45s); longer runs continue in the background. Each child that finishes while others are still running wakes you with <pi-famulus-wake kind="subagent-handover"> (its prompt and result). The whole run wakes you with <pi-famulus-wake kind="subagent-done">. Never poll or sleep to wait. A subagent still running past its timeout_ms is not stopped; it wakes you with <pi-famulus-wake kind="subagent-overrun"> so you can extend, steer, or interrupt it. Use action=list/get/status/interrupt/resume/steer/extend to manage existing runs.",
    "name": "subagent",
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": "list",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "get",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "status",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "interrupt",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "resume",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "steer",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "extend",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "models",
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Manage an existing run (or list selectable models) instead of starting a new one. When action is set, omit tasks and chain entirely; these launch-only fields are not required placeholders for control calls.",
        },
        "async": {
          "description": "Return immediately with a run_id; completion arrives via notification",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "chain": {
          "description": "Start a new sequential chain (always awaited). Use only when action is omitted. For any action call, omit chain entirely.",
          "items": {
