          "description": "Time budget per subagent turn in ms (default 1800000, max 3600000). Passing it does not stop the subagent: you get <pi-famulus-wake kind="subagent-overrun"> and choose extend, steer, or interrupt. With resume: the resumed turn's budget. With extend: the new budget from now.",
          "maximum": 3600000,
          "type": "number",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "promptGuidelines": [
      "When a <pi-famulus-wake kind="subagent-handover"> arrives, read <prompt> and <result> immediately and continue: subagent({action:"resume", run_id, child_id, message}) for that child, or agent_message to steer children that are still running. Do not wait for the rest of the run.",
      "Subagent runs that exceed the foreground budget continue in the background; you are notified per finished child and again when the run completes — do not poll.",
      "A failed subagent does not fail the whole run; inspect per-subagent sections in the result.",
      "<pi-famulus-wake> is a system wake, not a user reply. kind=subagent-handover is one child; kind=subagent-done is the whole run.",
    ],
    "promptSnippet": "Fan out subagents in parallel or sequence them in a chain",
  },
  {
    "description": "Message your subagents. "send" steers or queues a running child, and starts a new turn on an idle one. An idle child (warm or parked) continues with send or subagent resume; its prompt cache stays warm only for the time a wake or list reports. "reply" answers a child's pending decision request; "broadcast" steers every running child of a run (to = run_id); "list" shows children, pending decision requests, and recent traffic.",
    "name": "agent_message",
